  "text": "**Ruling out Solutions 1 and 2:** The KPZ line ensemble is strictly ordered, so H_n(x) > H_{n+1}(x) almost surely. That makes e^{H_{n+1}(x) - H_n(x)} < 1 pointwise, so its expectation must be strictly less than 1. Solution 2's answer of 1 is therefore impossible. Solution 1's answer of 1/t is also impossible for all t > 0, since it exceeds 1 when t < 1 and the problem asks for a value valid for every t.\n\n**Solution 3:** Its answer of 1/2 is consistent with the constraints above, since it lies in (0, 1). Its derivation is not rigorous: the \"Ward-type identity\" and \"energy sum rule\" are asserted rather than computed, and I could not verify the value from first principles here. It is plausible as the intended constant, and it is the only candidate that survives the basic checks, so I select it with moderate confidence.\n\nCHOICE: 3",
